<p>Hey there,</p>
<p>Quick heads up: we skipped last Friday, so it's been two weeks since #3. Good news is you didn't miss much on rates. The bigger story this time is what your loan actually costs once points, fees, and draws pile on, because it's a lot more than the rate on the term sheet.</p>
<h2>This week's published fix-and-flip rates</h2>
<p>Every number below comes from the lender's own public page. Our last check was <strong>Nov 13, 2026</strong>. None of the 8 lenders we could check changed their published rate since <a href="issue-3.html">issue #3</a> (Oct 30), so that's four straight weeks with no moves. The one change: Xoan Capital's website went down (details below the table).</p>
